// M4NICE item 3: the `word` EXPORT — the opaque-Word seat of §2.5, and the
// end-to-end pin of the UNCALLABILITY claim the whole `word`-is-opaque design
// rests on.
//
// `poke : word -> val` declares a RAW-WORD parameter.  Mid.QbeModule's
// `exportScheme` maps the `word` atom to the RIGID opaque type `TCon "Word" []`
// (NOT a fresh variable, which is what `val` gets), so no Osier value inhabits
// it: a concrete argument is a LOUD `CannotUnify` by NAME MISMATCH
// (Type/Unify.elm:354-356), and an unannotated literal (`5 : number`) is a
// LOUD `FlexConflict` — `bindVar`'s `propagate FNumber` refuses any non-Int/
// Float binding (Type/Unify.elm:491-497,708-719).  importtab.elm's sibling
// `wordimp.elm` (this file's other caller) exercises exactly that: it is the
// qbe-check-level pin of the refusal; before it there was only a TestMain
// unit row pinning the SCHEME MAPPING and unifier rows pinning the two facts,
// and nothing pinning the composition.
//
// The body is deliberately trivial (the row is the CALL-SITE refusal, not a
// behaviour) but must be a VALID defun: an invalid body here would fail the
// .mid for an unrelated reason and the refusal message would stop naming the
// unifier.
module Wordy
export Wordy.poke : word -> val
defun Wordy.poke(w: word) -> val {
  return mknum(0);
}
